  "summary": "The saved mask (C42) comes from final_state.npz written by C36, which reads region_cube.npz (C26, all 4120 daily files, with the truncated 2000-05-21 file re-downloaded in C25) and pool_rows.pkl (C31). It computes per-cell Hazen p90 thresholds over \u00b15-day pools, smooths them with a circular cumsum-based 31-day mean, compares all 92 target days against them, and applies run/gap logic. Because the smoothing uses a cumulative sum, the target-day thresholds (doys 153\u2013244) take as inputs raw thresholds for doys 1\u2013259 and 352\u2013366. Their pools cover each baseline year's 1 Jan\u201320 Sep and 12\u201331 Dec."
